    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d685">

                <pb facs="0671" n="665" xml:id="pg665"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr.
                            von Holleben.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-12-24"><hi rendition="#italic">December 24,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Replying to your esteemed note of the 13th
                    instant, in which you state that the British Government has sent one of its war
                    vessels to cooperate in the protection of life and property in Samoa, and that
                    the German cruiser <hi rendition="#italic">Buzzard</hi> is already at Apia, I
                    have the honor to inform you that, in accordance with my note of November 3 to
                    Baron Ketteler, the United States steamship <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Alliance</hi> sailed for Samoa from Honolulu November 26. I am still
                    awaiting, but hope to receive soon the report from the American consul at Apia
                    to which I adverted in that note.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John W. Foster.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
